# Tier 1 monitoring redesign (CLAUDE.md "Session update ... 2026-09-04,
# spec/playbook v76") — fires trading-bot-digest.service at 21:30 UTC,
# weekdays only, per the milestone brief ("30 minutes after Track B/
# Track C's shared 21:00 UTC slot, so both daily jobs have finished
# first").
#
# FLAGGED, NOT SILENTLY RESOLVED: this is a literal, fixed-UTC schedule —
# unlike trading-bot-daily.timer / trading-bot-track-c.timer, which are
# both anchored to `17:00:00 America/New_York` (a timezone-aware
# OnCalendar= that stays pinned to market close year-round). 17:00
# America/New_York is 21:00 UTC only during Eastern Daylight Time (UTC-4,
# roughly mid-March to early November); during Eastern Standard Time
# (UTC-5), the two daily jobs actually fire at 22:00 UTC, not 21:00. A
# fixed 21:30 UTC digest slot is therefore only genuinely "30 minutes
# after" the other two jobs during EDT — during EST it would fire 30
# minutes BEFORE they run, defeating the ordering this timer exists to
# guarantee. The milestone brief specified 21:30 UTC literally, so that
# is what's implemented here — this comment records the DST-drift
# consequence for a droplet-side/claude.ai decision on whether to switch
# this to the same `America/New_York`-relative anchoring the other two
# timers use, rather than silently "fixing" it unbriefed.
#
# Requires systemd >= 239 for the per-line OnCalendar= timezone suffix —
# see trading-bot-daily.timer's header for the older-systemd fallback.
[Unit]
Description=Run trading-bot-digest.service every weekday, 30 minutes after the shared daily post-close slot

[Timer]
OnCalendar=Mon..Fri *-*-* 21:30:00 UTC
Persistent=false
AccuracySec=1min

[Install]
WantedBy=timers.target
